Below is a **step‑by‑step guide** you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for your e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole stack – from design to deployment – and give you concrete code snippets, folder layouts, and tool recommendations.  

---

## 1. Define the Scope & Gather Requirements

| Item | Why it matters | Typical outcome |
|------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, cart, checkout, user accounts, reviews, admin panel | List of pages & components |
| **Performance goals** | Fast first paint, low bundle size | Target metrics (e.g., < 2 s on 3G) |
| **SEO & Accessibility** | Google ranking, inclusive UX | WCAG 2.1 AA compliance |
| **Payment & Security** | PCI‑DSS, GDPR | Integration plan with Stripe/PayPal, secure auth |
| **Analytics** | Conversion tracking | GA4, Hotjar, custom events |

> **Tip:** Create a *feature matrix* (feature vs. priority) to keep the scope manageable.

---

## 2. Choose the Tech Stack

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular | **React** (most community, ecosystem) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil | **Redux Toolkit** (predictable, devtools) |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS, Styled‑Components, Emotion | **Tailwind** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Component library** | Material‑UI, Ant Design, Chakra UI | **Chakra UI** (accessibility out‑of‑the‑box) |
| **Routing** | React Router | ✅ |
| **Data fetching** | RTK Query, SWR, React Query | **RTK Query** (integrated with Redux) |
| **Type system** | TypeScript | ✅ |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | ✅ |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | ✅ |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (auto‑preview, edge functions) |
| **Build** | Vite, Next.js | **Next.js** (SSR + SSG + API routes) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Server‑side rendering → SEO & faster first paint.  
> • Static generation for product pages → instant load.  
> • API routes → you can keep the backend in the same repo.  
> • Edge functions → low‑latency auth, payment hooks.

---

## 3. Wireframe & Design

1. **Sketch** the main pages:  
   - Home / Landing  
   - Category / Search results  
   - Product detail  
   - Cart & Checkout  
   - User account (orders, profile)  
   - Admin dashboard (products, orders, analytics)

2. **Prototype** in Figma or Adobe XD.  
   - Use a design system (colors, typography, spacing).  
   - Export assets (icons, images) in SVG/PNG.

3. **Accessibility audit** (axe, Lighthouse).  
   - Ensure color contrast, semantic HTML, ARIA labels.

---

## 4. Project Skeleton (Next.js + TypeScript)

```
